{"kind":"assert","text":"M1a encoding, answer to 1f173a76. Ruling 900dd271 is reaffirmed in full, and this act replaces it as the effective ruling. The encoding is from: { kind, under, pin, at: { of: \"also.root\", slot } }, with to: \"outside\" on the endpoint connection and the full native ScopeRef supplied at installation. No new ScopeRef kind, journal record class or composition member is added, so the kernel filing gate does not hold it.\n\nEvery condition of 900dd271 stands:\n- Omitting at still refuses as unreachable-handler. That is the distinguishing control.\n- A missing, mutable, nullable, wrongly typed or conditionally initialized slot refuses as unbound-endpoint. Unknown at syntax, a missing under or pin, and non-tell use each refuse by name.\n- A different verified sender under the same pin refuses as not-the-sender, with one deciding entry, one result and zero handler effects (99f628a5).\n- From objects without at keep their exact bytes and behavior.\n- The M1a note carries its two limit sentences: the pin binds one sender definition digest, and M1b's many-sender direction stays open.\n\nIsolate the four M1a commits onto current main, reconcile the validator, and run the two-room witness. Name in the review request any change the reconcile needed beyond a rebase. No live room, deployment or Worker configuration change.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}